  "question": {
    "text": "An equilateral triangular loop <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> of uniform specific resistivity having some resistance is pulled with a constant velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> out of a uniform magnetic field directed into the paper. At time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, side <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> of the loop is at the edge of the magnetic field. The induced current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>I</mi></mfenced></math> versus time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> graph will be as :<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image10-9ac8c52e-4064-408c-939f-2f1846ed8010.jpg\" style=\"height: 139px; width: 180px;\" />",
